verses.text:
“Before I formed you in the belly I knew you,
and before you came out from the womb I set you apart;
a prophet to the nations I appointed you.”

Yet Yahweh answered me,
“Say not, ‘A youth am I’;
for wherever I send you, there you must go,
and whatever I bid you, that you must speak.

Holy was Israel to Yahweh,
the firstfruits of his harvest;
all who devoured him were held guilty;
disaster came upon them,’ declares Yahweh.”

And I brought you into a land of orchards,{d}
to eat its fruit and its good things;
but you came in and defiled my land,
and my heritage you made an abomination.

The priests never asked, ‘Where is Yahweh?’
Those who wield the law knew me not;
the shepherds{e} rebelled against me;
the prophets spoke by Baal{f}
and pursued what brings no gain.

Over him the young lions have roared;
they have lifted up their voice.
They have made his land a waste;
his cities are burned, without inhabitant.

And now, what have you to do with the road to Egypt,
to drink the waters of the Shihor?{m}
Or what have you to do with the road to Assyria,
to drink the waters of the River?{n}

Your own evil will discipline you,
and your turnings away will rebuke you.
Know then and see that it is evil and bitter
for you to forsake Yahweh your God;
the dread of me is not in you,”
declares the Lord Yahweh of Armies.{o}

“How can you say, ‘I am not defiled;
after the Baals I have not gone’?
See your way in the valley;{p}
know what you have done—
a swift young she-camel
running crisscross on her paths,

Where then are those gods you made for yourself?
Up with them, if they can rescue you
when trouble comes;
for your gods have grown as many
as your towns, O Judah.{q}

O generation, you—see the word of Yahweh!
Have I been a wilderness to Israel,
or a land of thick darkness?{r}
Why do my people say, ‘We roam free;
we will come to you no more’?

Even in your skirts is found
the blood of the guiltless poor;
not as housebreakers did you find them.{s}
Yet in spite of all this

From there also you shall go out
with your hands upon your head;{t}
for Yahweh has rejected those in whom you trust,
and you shall not prosper through them.

Go and proclaim these words toward the north, and say,
‘Return, faithless Israel,’ declares Yahweh;
‘I will not let my face fall upon you in anger,
for faithful am I,’ declares Yahweh;
‘I will not keep anger forever.

Let us lie down in our shame,
and let our disgrace cover us;
for against Yahweh our God we have sinned,
we and our fathers,
from our youth even to this day,
and we have not obeyed the voice of Yahweh our God.”

Raise a signal toward Zion;
flee for safety; do not stand still,
for I am bringing disaster from the north,
and a great destruction.

Up from his thicket the lion has gone,
the ravager of nations is on the march;
out from his place he has come
to turn your land into a waste;
your towns shall lie in ruins, empty of people.

My bowels, my bowels!{d} I writhe in pain!
O the walls of my heart!
My heart moans within me;
I cannot keep silent,
for the sound of the ram’s horn you have heard, O my soul,
the alarm of war.

For thus says Yahweh:
“A desolation shall the whole land be;
yet a full end I will not make.

Because of this the land shall mourn,
and the sky above grow black;
for I have spoken it, I have determined it;
I will not relent, nor will I draw back.”

At the noise of horseman and archer
every city flees;
they go into thickets;
they climb among the rocks;
every city is forsaken,
and no man dwells in them.

O Yahweh, do not your eyes look for faithfulness?
You struck them, but they felt no grief;
you consumed them, but they refused to accept correction.
Harder than rock they made their faces;
they refused to turn back.

Then I said, “Surely these are only the poor;
they act foolishly,
for they know not Yahweh’s way,
the judgment of their God.

I will get me to the great ones
and speak with them,
for they know Yahweh’s way,
the judgment of their God.”
But these too had all alike shattered the yoke;
they had snapped the bonds.

Therefore a lion from the forest shall slay them;
a wolf of the desert plains shall ravage them;
a leopard keeps watch over their towns;
whoever goes out of them shall be torn in pieces,
because their transgressions are many,
mighty their acts of turning away.

Shall I not punish them for these things?” declares Yahweh;
“and on a nation such as this
shall my soul not take vengeance?

The prophets shall turn to wind;
the word is not in them.
So be it done to them!”

Your crops and your bread they will devour;
your sons and daughters they will devour;
your sheep and cattle they will devour;
your vine and fig they will devour;
the walled towns you rely on
they will batter down with the sword.

Will you not fear me?’ declares Yahweh.
‘Before me will you not tremble?
I placed the sand as the bound of the sea,
a perpetual decree it cannot pass;
though its waves toss, they cannot prevail;
though they roar, they cannot pass over it.

For among my people are found wicked men;
they watch like fowlers who crouch;{e}
they set a trap;
men they catch.

Like a cage full of birds,
so are their houses full of deceit;
therefore they have become great and grown rich.

They have grown fat and sleek;
they also overpass in deeds of evil;
they plead not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, that they may prosper,
and the right of the needy they do not defend.

Shall I not punish them for these things?’ declares Yahweh;
‘and on a nation such as this
shall my soul not take vengeance?’

Herdsmen with their flocks will march on her;
round about her they will pitch their tents;
each will crop his own patch.

For thus says Yahweh of Armies:
“Hew down her trees;
cast up a siege mound against Jerusalem.
This is the city to be punished;
oppression is all within her.

As a cistern keeps its water cool,
so she keeps her evil cool and fresh;
outrage and havoc echo in her;
sickness and blows are before my face continually.

But I am full of the wrath of Yahweh;
I am weary of holding it in.
“Pour it out upon the child in the street,
and upon the gathering of young men together;
for husband with wife shall be taken,
the elder with him who is full of days.

Did they feel shame for the loathsome things they did?
Not the least shame did they feel;
blushing they never learned.
So they will go down with the fallen;
when I call them to account they will be overthrown,” Yahweh has said.

Thus says Yahweh:
“See, a people comes from the land of the north;
a great nation is stirred up from the farthest parts of the earth.

Bow and javelin they grip;
cruel are they, and show no mercy;
their voice roars like the sea;
upon horses they ride,
arrayed as a man for battle
against you, O daughter of Zion.”

We have heard the report of it;
our hands hang limp;
anguish has seized us,
pain as of a woman in labor.

Venture not into the countryside,
nor travel the highway,
for the foe bears a sword;
dread surrounds on all sides.{g}

They are all stubborn rebels,
going about with slander;
bronze and iron are they;
all of them deal corruptly.

The bellows blow fiercely;
the lead is consumed by the fire;{i}
in vain the refiner refines,
for the wicked are not drawn off.

The wise men are put to shame;
they are dismayed and caught;
see, they have rejected the word of Yahweh,
so what wisdom is in them?

Therefore I will give their wives to others,
their fields to new owners;
for from the least to the greatest
every one is greedy for unjust gain;
from prophet to priest
every one deals falsely.

They have healed the wound of the daughter of my people lightly,
saying, “Peace, peace,”
when there is no peace.{b}

Were they ashamed when they committed abomination?
No, they were not at all ashamed;
they knew not how to blush.
Therefore they shall fall among those who fall;
in the time of their punishment they shall stumble,’ says Yahweh.

‘I will surely gather them in,’{c} declares Yahweh;
‘there are no grapes on the vine,
nor figs on the fig tree;
even the leaf has withered,
and what I gave them passes away from them.’”{d}

Why are we sitting here?
Assemble! Let us enter the walled towns
and meet our end there;
for Yahweh our God has sentenced us to die
and made us drink water laced with poison,{e}
since against Yahweh we have sinned.

They bend their tongue like their bow;
falsehood and not faithfulness has grown strong in the land;
for they proceed from evil to evil,
and me they do not know, declares Yahweh.

Guard yourselves, each against his friend,
and rely on no brother;
for each brother is a heel-grabber,{b}
and each friend peddles slander.

Each one deceives his neighbor,
and no one speaks the truth;
they have taught their tongue to speak lies;
they weary themselves committing iniquity.

A death-dealing arrow is their tongue;
treachery is its speech;
with his lips a man greets his friend with “Peace,”
but inwardly he plots to waylay him.

Over the hills I will lift up weeping and lament,
and over the wilderness grazing lands a dirge,
for they are scorched, with none passing through,
and no sound of cattle is heard;
the birds of the sky as well as the beasts
have fled away and gone.

Thus says Yahweh of Armies:
“Consider, and call for the mourning women to come;
send for the skillful women to come;

let them hurry and lift a dirge over us,
till our eyes stream with tears
and our lashes drip with water.

They adorn it with silver and with gold;
they fasten it with nails and hammers
so that it cannot move.

They are like a scarecrow in a melon patch,{a}
mute and unable to talk;
they must be hauled about,
having no power to walk.
Have no fear of them,
for harm is beyond them,
and good is beyond them too.”

Beaten silver is brought from Tarshish,
and gold from Uphaz,{c}
the work of the craftsman and of the hands of the goldsmith;
their clothing is blue and purple;
they are all the work of skilled men.

He made the earth by his power;
he established the world by his wisdom,
and by his understanding stretched out the heavens.

Every man is stupid, without knowledge;
every goldsmith is put to shame by his idol,
for his molten images are falsehood,
and there is no breath in them.

Not like these is the Portion of Jacob,{e}
for he is the Maker of all things,
and Israel is the tribe of his inheritance;
Yahweh of Armies is his name.

My tent is destroyed,
and all my cords are broken;
my children have gone from me,
and they are not;
there is no one to spread my tent again
and to set up my curtains.
